\section{Design}{

Each family/setting combination has 200 independent datasets, paired across
methods. The covariate is standard normal; Gaussian random intercepts have
variance 0.5. The true slope is 0.5, and the intercept is -0.5 for binary
responses and log(2) for Poisson. Binary responses are Bernoulli observations.

